          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "daily lives. And guess what happens as we discover more and more? We start realising that these ideas are all connected."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.144,
            0.581,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will start off by looking at our home, planet Earth. It is the only planet we know that supports life, and it has an environment that we must protect. There is an amazing variety of life on Earth—plants"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.606,
            0.103,
            0.752,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What will we explore with the help of this book?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.776,
            0.107,
            0.82,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.242,
            0.744,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and animals that have managed to survive and thrive in different regions on this planet. You might have seen a seed grow into a plant, a caterpillar transform into a beautiful butterfly and many more such observations. How do these plants and animals grow?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
